\cf2 \cb5 You are THREE experts analyzing a SaaS platform called CyberCheck. Give your analysis from each perspective.\
\
## EXPERT 1: SaaS Business Strategist\
Analyze the platform's business model, pricing, go-to-market strategy, and growth potential.\
\
## EXPERT 2: UX/UI Designer  \
Analyze the user experience from signup to daily use. What's the customer journey? Where will users get confused? What's missing?\
\
## EXPERT 3: Customer Experience Architect\
Analyze the end-to-end experience for ALL three user types: business owners, tourists/customers, and influencers.\
\
## THE PLATFORM:\
\
CyberCheck is THREE interconnected products:\
\
**Product 1: CyberCheck Dashboard** - Business management SaaS\
- Businesses sign up, get a dashboard with 28 feature modules\
- Includes: profile editor, media library, booking system, inventory/fleet management, availability calendar, customer CRM, coupons/promos, SMS marketing, waivers, waitlist, reviews, Stripe Connect payments, OAuth connections (42+ tools), theme customization, custom domain, site editor, publish system, billing\
- Each business gets a hosted website + linktree page that updates in real-time from dashboard edits\
- 11 marketplace apps available as paid add-ons (booking, SMS, loyalty, analytics, menu, ordering, social media, AI training, referrals, etc.)\
- The dashboard has 17 sidebar items currently - could be overwhelming for new users\
\
**Product 2: GCR (Gulf Coast Radar)** - Voice search engine for tourists\
- 296 hand-coded pages with 85+ real Gulf Coast businesses\
- Categories: restaurants (67), seafood (43), things to do (33), live music (21), nightlife (18), family fun (28), etc.\
- Goal: tourists talk to it or browse and find businesses with REAL-TIME AVAILABILITY (not just ratings)\
- Currently static HTML, needs to become database-driven\
- Has a voice search interface already built (Web Speech API)\
\
**Product 3: NoShoes Media** - Influencer referral network\
- Connects local influencers with businesses\
- Influencers get linktree pages with "My Picks" (referral links)\
- Businesses offer 10-12% commission per booking from influencer referrals\
- Business directory (premium vs free listings)\
- Influencer directory with verified creators\
\
**Revenue model:**\
- 1% platform fee on every payment (Stripe Connect)\
- Monthly subscriptions ($29-149/month)\
- Marketplace app subscriptions ($10-30/month each)\
- Premium GCR listings ($29-99/month)\
- Done-for-you setup ($299 one-time)\
- Commission cut from influencer referrals\
\
**Technical state:**\
- Express.js backend with Supabase - WORKING\
- JWT auth + Stripe Connect + Twilio SMS - WORKING\
- 60+ API endpoints - WORKING\
- Customer website fetches live data from API - WORKING\
- First customer handoff is TOMORROW\
\
**What already exists as UI designs (not all functional):**\
- 2,000+ HTML pages across 8 directories\
- Voice call management dashboard\
- AI chat assistant\
- Visual automation builder (drag-drop)\
- AI app builder (Lovable-style)\
- Developer portal with sandbox code editor\
- E-commerce storefront templates\
- 58 industry-specific linktree templates\
- Complete admin panel with GCR management\
\
## GIVE YOUR ANALYSIS:\
\
### From EXPERT 1 (SaaS Strategist):\
1. What's the strongest competitive advantage?\
2. What should the pricing tiers actually look like?\
3. What's the fastest path to $10K MRR?\
4. What feature should they NOT build (waste of time)?\
5. What's the #1 thing that will make or break this platform?\
\
### From EXPERT 2 (UX Designer):\
1. What's the ideal signup-to-first-value flow? (step by step)\
2. How should the dashboard be organized so it's not overwhelming?\
3. What should the mobile experience look like?\
4. What's the biggest UX problem in the current design?\
5. How should the linktree page builder work for non-technical users?\
\
### From EXPERT 3 (Customer Experience):\
1. Map the complete customer journey for a business owner (from hearing about CyberCheck to being a power user)\
2. Map the complete tourist journey (from wanting dinner to leaving a review)\
3. Map the complete influencer journey (from signing up to getting their first commission check)\
4. Where does each journey break down right now?\
5. What's the "aha moment" for each user type?\
\
Be specific, actionable, and opinionated. Don't hedge. Tell the founder exactly what to do.\cb1 \
