\f1\b\fs39 \cf2 THE ARCHITECTURE (How Everything Connects)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa304\partightenfactor0

\fs30\fsmilli15210 \cf2 Data Flow: Business Signs Up\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs26 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs23\fsmilli11700 \cf3 \cb4 1. Business visits cybercheck.com/signup\
2. Enters: email, password, business name, business type\
3. Backend creates: businesses row (site_id UUID, subdomain auto-generated)\
4. Backend creates: users row (linked via site_id, role=owner)\
5. Backend creates: site_content row (empty, ready for editing)\
6. Returns JWT token -> redirected to dashboard\
7. Dashboard loads -> all 28 modules available\
8. Business fills in profile, uploads photos, sets hours\
9. Each save calls CC.dashboard.updateX() -> PUT/POST to API -> Supabase\
10. Business clicks "Publish" -> their website goes live at subdomain.cybercheck.com\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa304\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs30\fsmilli15210 \cf2 \cb1 Data Flow: Dashboard Edit -> Live Website\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs26 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs23\fsmilli11700 \cf3 \cb4 Owner edits description in dashboard\
  -> profile.js calls CC.dashboard.updateProfile(\{description: "new text"\})\
  -> cc.js sends PUT /api/dashboard/profile with JWT header\
  -> auth middleware verifies JWT, attaches siteId\
  -> dashboard.js updates Supabase: site_content + businesses tables\
  -> Returns success\
\
Customer visits beachside.cybercheck.com\
  -> Site loads index.html (static template)\
  -> JS fetches GET /api/public/profile?subdomain=beachside-circle-boats\
  -> domain middleware resolves subdomain to site_id\
  -> public.js queries same Supabase tables\
  -> Returns fresh data -> site renders it\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa304\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs30\fsmilli15210 \cf2 \cb1 Data Flow: Customer Books on Website\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs26 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs23\fsmilli11700 \cf3 \cb4 1. Customer visits business website\
2. JS fetches fleet types, time slots, pricing, addons, availability\
3. Customer picks boat, date, time, addons\
4. POST /api/public/hold (10-min reservation hold, atomic stored procedure)\
5. Customer fills contact form, enters payment\
6. POST /api/public/bookings (full booking with customer + payment data)\
7. Backend: upserts customer, calls create_booking_if_available() stored procedure\
8. If Stripe connected: creates PaymentIntent via Stripe Connect\
   - application_fee_amount = 1% platform fee\
   - transfer_data.destination = business's connected Stripe account\
9. SMS to customer (booking confirmation via Twilio)\
10. SMS to business owner (new booking notification)\
11. Notification created in dashboard\
12. Owner sees booking in dashboard bookings tab\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa304\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs30\fsmilli15210 \cf2 \cb1 Data Flow: Influencer Referral\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs26 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs23\fsmilli11700 \cf3 \cb4 1. Influencer shares their NoShoes linktree URL with referral code\
2. Customer clicks "Beachside Circle Boats" on influencer's page\
3. Link includes ?ref=beachbilly-123 parameter\
4. Customer lands on business's booking page with referral tracked\
5. Customer books -> payment includes referral attribution\
6. Business pays commission (10-12%) to influencer\
